            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0669" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/353: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Greece</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-07T19:00:00-05:00">March 7, 1934—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Legation at Bucharest telegraphs that Rumanian Government has granted a
                    transit visa to Insull and that latter is expected in <pb facs="0670" n="570"
                        xml:id="pg570"/> Rumania within 48 hours. The American Ministers at
                    Bucharest, Sofia and Belgrade are being instructed to request Insull’s
                    provisional arrest and detention if and when he enters the territory of the
                    countries to which they are respectively accredited.</p>
                <p>Keep Department fully and promptly informed of developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
